---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import RedactText from '@/components/tools/redact/text/RedactText.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="redact-text" width="wide">
  <RedactText client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How to redact text</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Paste text into the box, or drop a .txt, .md, .csv, .json, .log or .eml file on it.</li>
      <li>The result updates as you type. Hidden items are shown as black marks with their replacement.</li>
      <li>Press a mark to keep that value visible everywhere in the text. Press it again to hide it.</li>
      <li>Choose what to hide and how to replace it. Add words the detectors missed to the always-hide list.</li>
      <li>Copy the result or download it as a .txt file.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What runs on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Two detectors run in your browser. Pattern rules find emails, phone numbers, card numbers (with the Luhn check), IBANs
      (with the mod 97 check), IP and MAC addresses, links, dates, postcodes, national ID numbers and more than 60 kinds of
      API keys and tokens. They work at once.
    </p>
    <p>
      A small language model finds names, street addresses, organizations, places, usernames and ID numbers that only the
      context gives away. It is a 19 MB file with a 14 MB runtime. Both download once from this site and
      are kept in your browser's storage, so the tool works offline after the first use. The model reads Latin-script text
      in English, German, French, Spanish, Italian, Dutch, Portuguese and Swedish best.
    </p>

    <h2>Replacement styles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Label: every name becomes [NAME], every email [EMAIL].</li>
      <li>Numbered label: each different value gets its own number, so [NAME 1] is always the same person.</li>
      <li>Block: a fixed row of squares that does not show the length of the value.</li>
      <li>Fake values: each person gets one realistic fake name, used every time they appear. "Anna Berg" and later "Anna" become "Laura Smith" and "Laura".</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to check that nothing is uploaded</h2>
    <p>
      Open your browser's developer tools, select the Network tab and paste your text. You see the model files load from
      this site the first time, and no request after that. You can also load the model once, turn off your network and use
      the tool.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No detector finds everything. Names in lower case, nicknames and rare spellings can be missed. Read the result before you share it.</li>
      <li>Some items are hidden that do not need to be. Press them to keep them.</li>
      <li>Very long texts take longer for the model: about one to three seconds for every 10,000 characters on a laptop. The pattern rules stay fast.</li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
